00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:07.510 align:start position:0%
the european union's competitiveness  council has adopted a new generation of  public and private partnerships  aimed at creating more jobs and boosting  economic growth  the partnerships will contribute to the  launch of large-scale and long-term  innovation projects  under the eu's massive new research  program horizon 2020  which was also formally adopted by the  ministers for the research community  horizon 2020 means valuable funding at a  time that many countries are struggling  to maintain science budgets  the new partnerships will focus on  innovative medicine  more effective diagnostics and  treatments with the aim of improving the  health and well-being of europeans  other partnerships include bio-based  industries aeronautics  electronics fuel cells and hydrogen  in public debate the council agreed a  general political approach  on the european program for monitoring  the earth from satellites  known as copernicus the program will be  used to support the agriculture and  fishery sectors  and will help in disaster response work  including fighting forest fires  elsewhere on the agenda ministers also  reached agreement on a common position  concerning new rules on breaches of  anti-trust laws  a challenge in the car industry among  other sectors  the proposals could make it easier for  victims of cartels  to receive compensation for loss of  business and lost profits
 

